From c74daf3245e31989ea3a78f02065ec7199b370c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:57:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] media: i2c: ov9282: add 1280x800 and 640x400 modes, Y8
 output (backport from v6.6)

Backport drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c from mainline v6.6. The 6.1 driver
has a single 1280x720 Y10_1X10 mode; the v6.6 driver adds:

  - 1280x800 (full array) and 640x400 (2x2 binned) modes alongside the
    existing 1280x720 mode, which stays the default;
  - 8-bit MEDIA_BUS_FMT_Y8_1X8 output next to Y10_1X10, with the
    pixel-rate control following the selected bit depth;
  - per-mode hblank/vblank limits and V4L2 selection (crop) targets;
  - the "ovti,ov9281" compatible, as the OV9281 is the same sensor
    with a different CRA.

The link frequency stays 400 MHz on 2 data lanes for every mode and
format. The 6.1 tree already has the subdev ops the v6.6 source uses
(init_cfg, v4l2_subdev_get_try_format/crop), so the only change is .probe to
.probe_new for the 6.1 i2c_driver API.

Upstream-Status: Backport [v6.6 drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c]
Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
